---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';

const base = import.meta.env.BASE_URL.replace(/\/$/, '');
const internal = (segment) => `${base}/${segment.replace(/^\//, '')}`;

const sequence = [
  ['01', 'The Authorial Capacity Constraint', 'Exploratory working paper', 'v0.2 · published', internal('publications/authorial-capacity-constraint')],
  ['02', 'Agalmic Economics: The Law of Displaced Scarcity', 'Foundational paper', 'Next', null],
  ['03', 'Innovation as Search', 'Exploratory paper', 'First sequence', null],
  ['04', 'Attention After Abundance', 'Working paper', 'Research track', null],
  ['05', 'Markets for Possibility', 'Working paper', 'Research track', null],
  ['06', 'Representation as Discovery', 'Research paper + software', 'Nemosyne track', null],
  ['07', 'Intellectual Property After Epistemic Abundance', 'Policy / economics paper', 'Research track', null],
];

const drafts = [
  ['Epistemic Handoff: Contribution, Authority and Uptake Under Cognitive Abundance', 'Substantial exploratory draft', internal('drafts/epistemic-handoff')],
  ['Credit Without Authority', 'Paper idea', null],
  ['Epistemic Uptake: The New Bottleneck in an Economy of Abundant Ideas', 'Paper idea', null],
  ['Markets for Expert Attention', 'Paper idea', null],
  ['The Human-Scale Epistemic Horizon', 'Deep-future paper idea', null],
];
---
<Layout title="Publications" description="The publication strategy, working papers and draft sequence for Agalmic Research.">
  <header class="page-head">
    <div class="shell">
      <p class="eyebrow">Publications</p>
      <h1>One research object. Many useful forms.</h1>
      <p class="lede">The paper is important, but it is not sacred. A durable research object can be projected into the format that best reaches the people who need to test, criticise, cite or build on it.</p>
    </div>
  </header>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="shell split">
      <div>
        <p class="eyebrow">Epistemic status</p>
        <h2>Publication is not certification.</h2>
      </div>
      <div class="prose">
        <p class="large">A public artefact can be valuable before its curator can defend every part of it.</p>
        <p>Agalmic Research uses machine cognition extensively. Each substantial publication should therefore disclose the kind of support it has actually earned rather than allowing polish to stand in for authority.</p>
        <div class="callout">
          <p><strong>Epistemic authority should not exceed defensibility.</strong> Exploratory work is published to be challenged, not to imply mastery.</p>
        </div>
        <p><a href={internal('publications/authorial-capacity-constraint')}>Read Working Paper 001: The Authorial Capacity Constraint →</a></p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="shell split">
      <div>
        <p class="eyebrow">Contribution & authority</p>
        <h2>Preserve the idea. Recruit the missing expertise.</h2>
      </div>
      <div class="prose">
        <p class="large">Origin deserves credit. Authority requires warrant.</p>
        <p>A promising contribution should not be discarded merely because its initiator lacks domain authority. Nor should initiation be mistaken for validation. The publication architecture is evolving toward separate records of contribution provenance and epistemic authority, with explicit handoffs between initiators, developers, domain stewards, verifiers and realizers.</p>
        <p><a href={internal('drafts/epistemic-handoff')}>Read the Epistemic Handoff draft →</a></p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="shell split">
      <div>
        <p class="eyebrow">Publication architecture</p>
        <h2>Record first. Refine continuously.</h2>
      </div>
      <div class="prose">
        <p class="large">Working paper → peer-reviewed article → public essay → policy brief → talk → model → code.</p>
        <p class="muted">These are views of the same evolving work, not seven disconnected content products. Stable versions should be archived with persistent identifiers where appropriate, while the living source remains openly inspectable.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="shell">
      <div class="section-head">
        <span class="section-number">Initial sequence</span>
        <div class="section-copy">
          <h2>The first paper family.</h2>
          <p>The numbered sequence begins with the epistemic conditions under which the programme itself is being produced. Agalmic Economics follows once the standard of stewardship has been made explicit.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="index-list">
        {sequence.map(([n, title, type, status, href]) => (
          <article class="index-item">
            <span class="index-meta">{n}</span>
            <div>
              <h3>{href ? <a href={href}>{title}</a> : title}</h3>
              <p class="muted">{type}</p>
            </div>
            <span class="index-status">{status}</span>
          </article>
        ))}
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="shell">
      <div class="section-head">
        <span class="section-number">Draft notebook</span>
        <div class="section-copy">
          <h2>Research directions before sequence.</h2>
          <p>Drafts preserve promising ideas without prematurely promoting them into the numbered publication sequence. Their status is deliberately visible.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="index-list">
        {drafts.map(([title, status, href], i) => (
          <article class="index-item">
            <span class="index-meta">D{String(i + 1).padStart(2, '0')}</span>
            <div>
              <h3>{href ? <a href={href}>{title}</a> : title}</h3>
              <p class="muted">Conceptual development / future research</p>
            </div>
            <span class="index-status">{status}</span>
          </article>
        ))}
      </div>
      <div class="actions">
        <a class="button secondary" href={internal('drafts')}>Browse all drafts & ideas</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="shell split">
      <div>
        <p class="eyebrow">Distribution</p>
        <h2>Make the work easy to find, cite and contest.</h2>
      </div>
      <div class="prose">
        <ul>
          <li><strong>Website:</strong> canonical index, summaries, revisions, epistemic status, contribution provenance and links between research threads.</li>
          <li><strong>GitHub:</strong> source, models, data, code, version history and public critique.</li>
          <li><strong>Research archives:</strong> stable snapshots through services such as Zenodo, OSF or SSRN where suitable.</li>
          <li><strong>Peer review:</strong> journal submission selected paper by paper, not as the only route to legitimacy.</li>
          <li><strong>Public writing:</strong> essays that expose the ideas to a wider intellectual market without diluting the underlying work.</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</Layout>
